    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_088b3414495b30c886f80af802677e4d2a4e7cc2aad6e47f9281be2e640e705f",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The line sigma=3/4 recurs at several logically separate proof sites. The introductory consequences expose convergence of an infinite main-term series; the full Voronoi/Bessel expansion has its own convergence boundary; continuation of the difficult g4 component reaches the target line only under the same restriction; the saddle treatment requires absolute convergence of its accumulated remainder; and the final cutoff removal and a residual component sum again invoke sigma<3/4. The repeated boundary is therefore tied to multiple series, continuation, and limit-passage obligations rather than appearing only as an arbitrary range attached to the final theorem.",
